    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d86-a1">

                <pb facs="0179" n="97" sameAs="frus:frus1911/pg97"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure—Translation.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Cuban Secretary of State to the American
                        Minister.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Habana</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian" when="1911-10-25"
                                ><hi rendition="#italic">October 25,
                    1911</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>Mr. <hi rendition="#small-caps">Minister</hi>: In continuation of the
                    conversation that I had the honor to have with your excellency a few days ago, I
                    beg that you will inquire of your Government if it considers it convenient and
                    immediately feasible to agree with that of Cuba upon the extension for another
                    five years of the treaty of commercial reciprocity that is still in force,
                    though automatically; and if it would be willing to enter into negotiations with
                    a view to the modfication of the treaty in the sense of providing for greater
                    advantages for some American products and for our sugars and tobacco.</p>
                <p>I avail, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Manuel Sanguily.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
